{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For the et is elided.</b> Now it has been explained: וְאָסַפְתֶּם אֶת־תְּבוּאָתְכֶם (and you shall gather your produce) from field and vineyard." "<b>לָשֶׂבַע.</b> A verb." "<b>לָבֶטַח.</b> With lamed, and without it it is the same. So too the word לְבַדָּד. Now he mentioned satiety first, for it is the main thing." "And the meaning of <b>וִישַׁבְתֶּם לָבֶטַח</b> is that in years of famine people are driven from their place, as in the sense of לֹא־תֹסִיף תֵּת כֹּחָהּ לָךְ נַע וָנָד (you shall no longer give it strength to you, wandering and straying)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:38.481416079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}